  "published": "1900-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.0.0 — BREAKING. See MIGRATION.md for rationale and restoration steps. Breaking: (1) `ClientIp` no longer trusts `X-Forwarded-For` by default; it now comes from `Connection.RemoteIpAddress` (opt back in via `TrustForwardedHeaders: true`). (2) New redacted `ForwardedFor` property on request summaries when `X-Forwarded-For` is present. (3) `MaxBodyCaptureBytes <= 0` now fails at startup (`OptionsValidationException`) instead of silently disabling body capture. (4) Request bodies are now captured for failing (5xx) requests even before step-up engages. (5) `jti` and `User-Agent` now pass through `RedactionRegexes`. Non-breaking fixes: bodies redacted before truncation; `RegexOptions.NonBacktracking` redaction compilation; OTLP header/attribute percent-decoding; no double-exported summaries; `reloadOnChange` restored for config-declared sinks; one `ApplyRedaction` span per request. New options: `TrustForwardedHeaders` (default `false`), `MaxContinuousStepUpSeconds` (default `0`), `StepUpCooldownSeconds` (default `300`).",
